        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void isotp_link_receive</definition>
        <argsstring>(struct isotp_link *link, const uint8_t *data, size_t length, uint32_t now_us)</argsstring>
        <name>isotp_link_receive</name>
        <param>
          <type>struct <ref refid="structisotp__link" kindref="compound">isotp_link</ref> *</type>
          <declname>link</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const uint8_t *</type>
          <declname>data</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>size_t</type>
          <declname>length</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>uint32_t</type>
          <declname>now_us</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Process one received CAN frame addressed to this link. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Single Frames and the last Consecutive Frame complete a message and call the message handler. A First Frame is answered with a Flow Control frame. Malformed frames are ignored and counted; unexpected Consecutive and Flow Control frames are ignored. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>link</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Link state. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>data</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>CAN frame data. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>length</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>CAN data length, 1..8. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>now_us</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Current time in microseconds (free-running, wraps at 2^32). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
